    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the rule: **a supplied `registrationDate` later than the server date is rejected with HTTP 400**, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (not Spring MVC controllers).\n\nChanges to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline:\n\n1. **`ValidateOwnerRegistrationDate`** (new function class) \u2014 reads the validated body via `@Val OwnerFieldsDto` and throws a checked `FutureRegistrationDateException` when `registrationDate` is present and after `LocalDate.now()`. An absent date is skipped (it defaults to today at build time), preserving the existing contract.\n\n2. **`FutureRegistrationDateException`** (new checked exception) \u2014 so it appears in the `throws` clause and can be handled by escalation.\n\n3. **`FutureRegistrationDateExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML (`officefloor/escalation/\u2026FutureRegistrationDateException.yml`) \u2014 responds `400 Bad Request` with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing `InvalidPostcodeException` handler.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `validateRegistrationDate` step right after `validate`, so an invalid future date is rejected early, before any load/normalization work.\n\nThe new `errorRejectsFutureDate` test (posting `registrationDate: 2999-01-01`) passes, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
